          <toggle-section open="false">
            <h3>Video transcript </h3>
            <p><strong>Leah:</strong> Quite a lot of the time the focus of effective teamwork relates to have good working relationships with other members of the team and while this is critical to the successful completion of projects, what about relationships with other teams?</p>
<p><strong>Chris:</strong> It is just as important to develop good working relationships with other teams as there are very few instances when a project relies solely on the input and output of one team. To successfully complete a project there will likely be several teams working on different elements.</p>
<p><strong>Leah:</strong> As we mentioned in session 1, when working in an ‘Agile’ environment, projects will involve teams with a variety of skillsets who will work on different elements of a project. These teams will rely on each other as the project progresses and frequently use ‘Scrum’ and ‘Kanban’ methodologies to track progress across the teams. This enables the teams to monitor progress and identify any potential risks or holdups and develop solutions to move forward.</p>
<p><strong>Chris:</strong> Multi team projects can help to maintain effective and develop positive working relationships. This way you can gain a holistic view of the project and working with other teams on collaborative projects are also a useful way to gain an understanding about the organisation’s other moving parts, and how those parts can work together to better achieve the organisation’s mission. When members of different teams communicate frequently, you should always feel able to ask questions and have a firm grasp of the nature of one another’s work and therefore productivity is considerably boosted.</p>
<p><strong>Leah:</strong> Collaborative work also allows team members to bring their individual work styles, skills, and perspectives to projects which creates opportunities for new solutions and better results.</p>
<p>Imagine not knowing that the perfect approach, team member, or resource for a task your team is stuck on, has been under your nose the entire time.</p>
<p><strong>Chris:</strong> Good communication provides opportunities to improve your own teams’ methodologies. When teams from different departments are transparent about how they work, it gives you the opportunity to review the way you do your own work which can highlight any weaknesses that you or another team might have. When working together, take note of what questions others ask about your department, what is confusing to them about the way you do your work, and consider how that might help you to find ways to improve your own ways of working.</p>
<p><strong>Leah:</strong> It can also help you to gain a greater sense of the challenges that might be faced in terms of deadlines and discover ways you can continue to support one another, coordinate your work with each other, and provide support to others.</p>

          </toggle-section>
        
      
          
        </section>
        
    
     
    
  
     
    
  
  
        <section id="the-benefits-of-developing-positive-working-relationships-with-other-teams-and-departments"  class="t-bg-primary">
          
            <h2>The benefits of developing positive working relationships with other teams and departments</h2>
              <p>Being able to have positive working relationships with other teams and departments enables access to a wide range of skills and working methods which can provide a higher level of creativity and innovation.</p>
<p>Select the images below to read about some other important benefits.</p>

              
              <!-- IF 2 --><ul class="l-icon-grid ">
  
  
    
    <!--  -->
      
  
  
    
  
  <li class="c-reveal-block">
    <img class="c-reveal-block__icon js-showhide" src="~/images/svg/cp3/cp3_u1_s4_p1_reveal1.svg" alt="Increased efficiency" width="266" height="266">
    
    <div class="c-reveal-block__desc">
      <h3 aria-hidden="true">Increased efficiency</h3>
      <p>Cross team collaboration allows team members to focus on their own specialist skills while still having the opportunity to learn from each other. This can lead to increased efficiency and productivity across all teams.</p>

    </div>
  </li>
      
  
  
    
  
  <li class="c-reveal-block">
    <img class="c-reveal-block__icon js-showhide" src="~/images/svg/cp3/cp3_u1_s4_p1_reveal2.svg" alt="Improved performance" width="266" height="266">
    
    <div class="c-reveal-block__desc">
      <h3 aria-hidden="true">Improved performance</h3>
      <p>When employees focus on what they do best and don’t have to deal with tasks that are beyond their current skills or capabilities, they produce higher quality work.</p>

    </div>
  </li>
      
  
  
    
  
  <li class="c-reveal-block">
    <img class="c-reveal-block__icon js-showhide" src="~/images/svg/cp3/cp3_u1_s4_p1_reveal3.svg" alt="Increased competency" width="266" height="266">
    
    <div class="c-reveal-block__desc">
      <h3 aria-hidden="true">Increased competency</h3>
      <p>While collaboration enables individual team members to focus on their core competencies, it can also help to increase competencies. By collaborating with teams, team members learn more about what they do, and gain a broader understanding of the system they work within.</p>

    </div>
  </li>
      
  
  
    
  
  <li class="c-reveal-block">
    <img class="c-reveal-block__icon js-showhide" src="~/images/svg/cp3/cp3_u1_s4_p1_reveal4.svg" alt="Trust is built" width="266" height="266">
    
    <div class="c-reveal-block__desc">
      <h3 aria-hidden="true">Trust is built</h3>
      <p>Strong teams cultivate a foundation of trust. Trust maintains open lines of communication between all teams and team members which encourages people to share information.</p>

    </div>
  </li>
      
  
  
    
  
  <li class="c-reveal-block">
    <img class="c-reveal-block__icon js-showhide" src="~/images/svg/cp3/cp3_u1_s4_p1_reveal5.svg" alt="Reduced stress" width="266" height="266">
    
    <div class="c-reveal-block__desc">
      <h3 aria-hidden="true">Reduced stress</h3>
      <p>When employees try to do too many tasks, it can negatively affect their productivity and health. In a multi team environment, employees can support each other, reducing the likelihood of burnout.</p>

    </div>
  </li>
      
  
  
    
  
  <li class="c-reveal-block">
    <img class="c-reveal-block__icon js-showhide" src="~/images/svg/cp3/cp3_u1_s4_p1_reveal6.svg" alt="Leads to innovation" width="266" height="266">
    
    <div class="c-reveal-block__desc">
      <h3 aria-hidden="true">Leads to innovation</h3>
      <p>Most innovation comes as the result of the effort of a group or groups of people, rather than an individual. Most lasting innovations start with the creative process, which then moves through development, refinement, execution, and revision phases. Innovation usually involves input from many employees. The different experiences and perspectives of different teams can be utilised.</p>

    </div>
  </li>
      
  
  
    
  
  <li class="c-reveal-block">
    <img class="c-reveal-block__icon js-showhide" src="~/images/svg/cp3/cp3_u1_s4_p1_reveal7.svg" alt="Brings mutual support" width="266" height="266">
    
    <div class="c-reveal-block__desc">
      <h3 aria-hidden="true">Brings mutual support</h3>
      <p>When teams work well together they are also supportive of one another. Mutual support can encourage people to achieve goals they may not have realised they could reach on their own. Furthermore, teams offer an environment that provides a sense of belonging.</p>

    </div>
  </li>
      
  
  
    
  
  <li class="c-reveal-block">
    <img class="c-reveal-block__icon js-showhide" src="~/images/svg/cp3/cp3_u1_s4_p1_reveal8.svg" alt="Job satisfaction" width="266" height="266">
    
    <div class="c-reveal-block__desc">
      <h3 aria-hidden="true">Job satisfaction</h3>
      <p>The advantages of working with other teams and departments can lead to improved organisational efficiency and customer satisfaction. It also contributes to employees’ job satisfaction, through learning, reduced stress, more support and better use of skills. When employees are more satisfied, they tend to be motivated, less prone to absenteeism and more productive.</p>

    </div>
  </li>
      
  
  
    
  
  <li class="c-reveal-block">
    <img class="c-reveal-block__icon js-showhide" src="~/images/svg/cp3/cp3_u1_s4_p1_reveal9.svg" alt="Improved service" width="266" height="266">
    
    <div class="c-reveal-block__desc">
      <h3 aria-hidden="true">Improved service</h3>
      <p>In any successful organisation, there tends to be a strong team spirit that is appreciated by its internal customers, external customers and supporters. Having positive relationships with other teams leads to positive attitudes and a strong sense of commitment to the organisation. This in turn helps helps to maintain and improve the organisation's reputation for delivering quality products on time.</p>

    </div>
  </li>
  
</ul>

            
          
        </section>
        
    
     
    
  
  
